# Rust build artifacts
target/
dist/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Release tarball staging dirs (per-version, written by the release ceremony —
# multi-MB build-host artifacts; provenance lives in git tags + GitHub releases,
# not in source history).
/[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*/

# Local analysis / tooling scratch (knowledge-graph + dashboard)
.understand-anything/
.understand-anything-dashboard.log

# ESP images for testing
*.img
*.vhd

# OVMF temp vars
*_VARS.fd

# Editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Reports
reports/

# Backup files
*.bak
*.orig

# Signing keys — NEVER commit private key material
# All key-related directories are ignored; public certs are distributed via
# dist/ and release artifacts, not tracked in source. If you need to track a
# specific public cert, use `git add -f keys/<name>.crt` deliberately.
keys/
keys-gen/
keys-archive/
*.key
*.pem
*_priv*

# Root-level test signing artifacts (clean up stray certs from prior testing)
PK-*.pem
KEK-*.pem
db-*.pem

# Read-path test scratch files (manual FS read-contract probing, e.g.
# readtest17c.txt). Root-level throwaways — never part of the source tree.
readtest*.txt

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Test-fixture credential artifacts from archinstall runs.
# user_configuration.json (storage layout) is fine to commit; the
# credential files are not — even when the password is a throwaway
# test value, the file pattern is categorically credentials.
docs/test-fixtures/**/PASSWORDS.txt
docs/test-fixtures/**/user_credentials.json
